## III. HAWAII RULES OF PROFESSIONAL CONDUCT VIOLATIONS

| Rule | Standard | Violation | Evidence |
|------|----------|-----------|----------|
| **3.3(a)(1)** | Candor to Tribunal | False allegations of abuse/neglect submitted without verification | Affidavits contradicted by Grok/ChatGPT/audio |
| **3.4(a)** | Evidence Suppression | Concealment of exculpatory evidence during discovery | Grok/ChatGPT archives never disclosed; audio objected to without merit |
| **1.2(d)** | Assisting Client Crime | Facilitation of perjury & parental alienation | Mother coached child; false testimony accepted |
| **1.6 (Exception)** | Confidentiality Limits | Unlawful conduct (evidence suppression) not privileged | Conspiracy with Brower to deprive parental rights |
| **8.4(d)** | Prejudicial Conduct | Conduct prejudicial to administration of justice | Systematic evidence suppression + false allegations |
| **8.3(a)** | Reporting Duty | Failure to report judicial misconduct | Judge's bias known but unreported |
| **1.4** | Communication | Failed to communicate with opposing party re: exculpatory evidence | Grok/ChatGPT archives never provided |

